<p class="lp-small">Fathom Business requires two paid users. Avoma assigns one recording licence and one coaching add-on to each person. Other rows use the published per-user rate; confirm any Sybill or Dialpad seat minimum in the offer. AI packs, calling extras and optional setup are excluded.</p>
<div class="sg-two sg-after" id="gong-price"><div><h3>Gong pricing needs a full quote.</h3><p>Gong charges user licences plus a platform fee. Its current structure separates the core platform from applications for coaching, forecasting and outreach.</p><p>Selected advanced AI features also use credits. Get the required applications and expected usage priced alongside the seats.</p></div><div><h3>When is Gong worth keeping?</h3><p>Keep it when managers use its call reviews, coaching and deal data to run the sales team. A working system with valuable history can be worth more than a cheaper replacement.</p><p>If the team mostly opens summaries, a smaller tool deserves a trial. Paying for management features that nobody uses is poor value at any company size.</p></div></div>
{{ g.sources([['Gong pricing','https://www.gong.io/pricing'],['Current applications and seats','https://help.gong.io/docs/plans-and-seats'],['Gong AI credit rules','https://help.gong.io/docs/about-gong-credits']]) }}
<div class="lp-note"><strong>CallTeam verdict: ask for the price before the long demo.</strong><p>Quote-only pricing makes budgeting harder. Give sales your team size and required features, then ask for the first-year total and renewal terms. A product tour can wait until the budget makes sense.</p></div>
