<section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="switching"><div class="lp-wrap">
{{ g.heading('04','Use a real call before you commit','Test the workflow<br>before replacing Gong.','Choose a short cold call and a longer discovery meeting. They expose different recording, scoring and follow-up problems.') }}
<div class="sg-flow">
<div><h3>Capture the right calls.</h3><p>Use your actual dialler and meeting software. Check who gets recorded, whether both speakers appear correctly and how the record matches to the contact.</p></div>
<div><h3>Inspect the feedback.</h3><p>Compare the transcript with the audio. Look for missed objections, incorrect names and invented next steps. Ask the manager to turn the review into one specific practice exercise.</p></div>
<div><h3>Test the handoff.</h3><p>Check the CRM notes, fields and task owner. Export a recording and transcript. Confirm what happens to your old call library, scorecards and access when the contract ends.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="dg-callout"><h3>A useful review should change the next call.</h3><p>Suppose a rep explains the product after the buyer says they already have a supplier. Review that moment, practise a question about the current arrangement, then listen for how the rep handles it next time. A talk-time percentage alone gives the rep too little direction.</p><p>Our <a href="/services/sdr-training/">SDR coaching</a> connects the review to practice. Use the <a href="/cold-call-script-checker/">free script checker</a> to tighten the words before the session.</p></div>
<p class="dg-related">For a Gong migration, authorised users can download recording media and transcripts. Test a sample with the new provider before moving the archive; scorecards and playlists may need rebuilding. <a href="https://help.gong.io/v1/docs/take-action-on-a-call" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gong's export options ↗</a></p>
</div></section>
